      "dcterms:title": "LARGEST HYPERBOLIC ACTIONS OF 3–MANIFOLD GROUPS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "CAROLYNABBOTT, HOANG THANH NGUYEN",
        "RASMUSSEN, ALEXANDER J."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20230514",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.07425",
      "dcterms:abstract": "The set of equivalence classes of cobounded actions of a group G on diﬀerent hyperbolic metric spaces carries a natural partial order. Following Abbott–Balasubramanya– Osin, the group G is H–accessible if the resulting poset has a largest element. In this paper, we prove that every non-geometric 3-manifold has a ﬁnite cover with H–inaccessible fundamental group and give conditions under which the fundamental group of the original manifold is H– inaccessible. We also prove that every Croke-Kleiner admissible group (a class of graphs of groups that generalizes fundamental groups of 3–dimensional graph manifolds) has a ﬁnite index subgroup that is H–inaccessible.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2305.07425v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2305.07425v1"
    }
  ]
}
